  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core safety-services operations are exhibiting strong momentum, with record net revenues and robust organic growth across fire, life safety, and security end markets. Resilient demand is underpinned by secular trends in regulatory compliance and infrastructure maintenance. The company’s upbeat full-year guidance raise early in 2026 signals confidence that these demand conditions are sustainable, driving broad-based gains that extend well beyond any transient noise.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing an active consolidation strategy in a fragmented industry, recently adding Wtech Fire Group and targeting a step-change in scale by 2028. Credibility is reinforced by a pattern of raised guidance, expanding adjusted profitability, and candid investor-conference discussions that acknowledge regulatory challenges while detailing a clear growth roadmap. This consistent delivery has sustained favorable analyst commentary and buy ratings, with a prior non-recurring EPS distortion failing to dent the positive execution narrative.",
